  "notes": "West leads the ♥5 against 6♠. East wins the opening heart lead and returns the suit. South has a loser in both diamonds and clubs. Dummy's third heart will provide a discard for 1 of these losers. The diamond suit offers finessing possibilities for taking care of South's other loser.\n\nSouth should time his plays to take advantage of a possible 3-3 club break before taking the diamond finesse. South should begin by drawing trump. Next, he crosses to the dummy in clubs. North's remaining heart honour should be played for a club discard.\n\nSouth now cashes North's other club honour. A low club is led from the dummy and ruffed in the closed hand. When clubs prove to be 3-3, North has a long club established to take care of South's diamond loser. The ♦A is an entry to the club winner.\n\nIf clubs are 4-2, South takes the diamond finesse, hoping West was dealt the ♦K.",
